    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe registration-date business-day rule in `BuildOwner.java` now rolls forward past listed public holidays in addition to weekends.\n\n- Added the fixed public-holiday calendar as `PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS`: `2026-01-01`, `2026-01-26`, `2026-04-25`, `2026-12-25`, `2026-12-28`.\n- Rewrote `toBusinessDay` to loop forward one day at a time while the date is a weekend **or** a public holiday, returning the first date that is neither. This correctly chains adjustments \u2014 e.g. `2026-12-25` (Fri holiday) \u2192 skips the weekend \u2192 `2026-12-28` (also a holiday) \u2192 `2026-12-29` (Tue).\n- Factored the weekend check into an `isWeekend` helper and updated the surrounding comment.\n\nEverything derived from the registration date (membership-number year, daily create-limit) continues to see this adjusted business day, since the adjustment still happens before `built.set(owner)`.\n\nThe existing acceptance test (`coreDefaultDateIsBusinessDay`, which asserts the invariant that the default registration date is never a Saturday or Sunday) still passes: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
